T Chart                             | ChartPartition.h | 51-60   | owning                        | -  | One connected piece of topology bounded by seams and by the topology's own boundary. results on the partition revision, and a chart whose member set is unchanged keeps its least face ordinal — so a partition that touched one seam does not renumber every chart and discard every derived artefact for a change the artist cannot see.
    has   IdentityOrdinal   std::uint32_t               [-]  ?
    has   Faces             std::vector<std::uint32_t>  [-]  ?
    has   Cause             TerminationCause            [-]  ?
    has   ResidualNorm      double                      [-]  ?
    has   IterationCount    std::uint32_t               [-]  ?
    has   Distortion        DistortionMeasure           [-]  ?
    has   SubdivisionCount  std::uint32_t               [-]  ?
    by    Source/ChartPartition.cpp
    note  🔴 Chart identity is the **least imported face ordinal** the chart holds. `24` §3 keys transferred

