T DerivedPartition                  | ChartPartition.h | 90-97   | owning                        | -  | A whole derived partition, as a value that crosses back to the tick. `34` §3 requires the requester to apply the result on the tick. The previous partition stands until `Adopt` takes this one — a surface with no valid domain has no place to sample and nothing for `18` §1.1 to derive a tangent basis from, and the visible result of swapping mid-solve is the whole object flickering while an unrelated seam is being marked.
    has   Charts             std::vector<Chart>             [-]  ?
    has   CornerCoordinates  std::vector<DomainCoordinate>  [-]  ?
    has   DerivedSeams       std::vector<SeamEdge>          [-]  ?
    has   Metrics            PartitionMetrics               [-]  ?
    has   DescribedRevision  std::uint64_t                  [-]  ?
    by    Source/ChartPartition.cpp, Source/ConsoleHost.cpp
    note  🔴 A value rather than a mutation, because `68` §7 runs the flattening on `34`'s `Background` class and

//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                                     THE DERIVATION
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

F Derive                            | ChartPartition.h | 123     | api,nonthrowing               | 🔴 | Cuts, flattens and arranges one sealed topology into its parametric domain. ExtentExhausted when the conditioning describes another revision or no scale packs The `SeamSpecification` is taken by const reference and its derived set is returned in the result rather than written into it, so a worker running this touches no document state at all. and re-flatten, recording the crossing edges as derived seams. `68` §4.1 prescribes it for a fold, and a chart with two boundary loops is the same failure one step earlier. Subdivision strictly reduces the face count and a single face is always a disc that flattens without folding, so it terminates. `68` §7 puts this on `34`'s `Background` class; called on the tick it would stall a stroke.
    in    Imported      const TopologyStructure&       [-]  the sealed topology; immutable for the whole run
    in    Conditioned   const TopologyConditioning&    [-]  its conditioning, at the same revision
    in    Seams         const SeamSpecification&       [-]  the authored seams; the derived set is produced here and returned, not written back
    in    Declaring     const PartitionSpecification&  [-]  the parameters
    in    Cancellation  const WorkCancellation&        [-]  read between charts — `34` §5's cooperative points
    in    Progressed    WorkProgress&                  [-]  charts resolved out of charts spanned
    out   -             Outcome                        [-]  refuses with HostDenied for an unsealed topology or a withdrawn declaration, and with
    by    Api/CameraProjection.h, Api/IlluminantPopulation.h, Api/QuadratureIntegrator.h, Source/CameraProjection.cpp, Source/ChartPartition.cpp, Source/ConsoleHost.cpp, (+2 more)
    note  🔴 Reads nothing but its arguments and mutates none of them, which is exactly `34` §2's requirement.
    note  🔴 A chart that is not a disc and a chart that folds are answered by the **same** mechanism: subdivide
    note  ⚠️ The boundary self-intersection test is quadratic in boundary length. That is affordable only because

