T ChartPartition                    | ChartPartition.h | 143-193 | owning                        | -  | The partition a surface currently addresses, and the revision every derived artefact keys on. while `20` promotes against it. Re-partitioning moves domain positions, so every derived artefact addressed in the old domain is invalid — and the revision is what makes that discoverable rather than silent. rather than world-referred, which is `68` §6's table read from the storage side.
    has   StandingPartition  DerivedPartition  [-]  ?
    has   PartitionRevision  std::uint64_t     [-]  ?
    by    Source/ChartPartition.cpp, Source/ConsoleHost.cpp
    note  🔴 `68` §6: a re-partition advances the partition revision, and `24` §3 keys transferred results on it
    note  🔴 A camera move, an occupant move and a paint stroke re-derive nothing here. The domain is parametric

